home-workflow-eyebrow = Less glue. Explicit contracts.
home-workflow-title = Your project has a rhythm. Make it repeatable.
home-workflow-description = Keep orchestration, environment inputs, repository conventions, and procedural scripts distinct instead of tangling them into one language. Start with workspace.flow alone and add the rest only when needed.
home-workflow-link = Why Everyinit & architecture
home-workflow-compare-link = Compare with mise, Task & just
home-contract-one-kind = WORKFLOW
home-contract-one-file = .evin/workspace.flow
home-contract-one-title = Tasks, stages, and hooks
home-contract-one-description = The only required file. Declare project commands and dependencies once, then reuse that graph locally, in hooks, and in CI.
home-contract-two-kind = ENVIRONMENT · OPTIONAL
home-contract-two-file = .evin/environment.json
home-contract-two-title = Typed inputs and presets
home-contract-two-description = Define required variables, defaults, stage scopes, and secret output redaction without storing credentials in Git.
home-contract-three-kind = POLICY · OPTIONAL
home-contract-three-file = .evin/policy.json
home-contract-three-title = Shared repository rules
home-contract-three-description = Keep commit formats, branch checks, and SemVer release rules together for local hooks and release automation.
home-contract-four-label = 04 / SCRIPT · *.esh
home-contract-four-copy = Structured scripts for branching, data, and cleanup.

home-trust-eyebrow = Execution · Built on explicit contracts
home-trust-title = Know what runs. Know what it can access.
home-trust-description = Understand how Everyinit validates configuration, scopes environment variables, supervises child process groups, and integrates with your repository before running a task.
home-trust-disclaimer = Everyinit provides orchestration and process-group supervision, not security sandboxing or automatic rollback.
home-trust-cta = Execution & trust model
home-trust-verify = Verify downloads
home-trust-one-label = 01 / INSPECTABILITY
home-trust-one-title = Inspect before executing
home-trust-one-description = Validate manifests with evin check, inspect resolved inputs with evin explain, and preview plans with --dry-run—read-only, with no tasks run or trace files written.
home-trust-two-label = 02 / BOUNDARIES
home-trust-two-title = Explicit user-space inputs
home-trust-two-description = Evin never requests elevated privileges itself (though tasks may invoke tools that do). Scope task variables with presets and pure: true, with *** output redaction.
home-trust-three-label = 03 / VERIFIABILITY
home-trust-three-title = Supervised runs, signed releases
home-trust-three-description = Deterministic DAG order, supervised process-group cleanup on failure or Ctrl+C, and Ed25519-signed SHA256SUMS release manifests.
home-trust-four-label = 04 / REVERSIBILITY
home-trust-four-title = Reversible integration
home-trust-four-description = Keep existing cargo, npm, or shell commands in .evin/workspace.flow and isolate hook shims inside EVIN markers. Porting custom .esh logic later still takes effort.

